WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.732
Do not give every tool to the model on every turn.

00:00:03.732 --> 00:00:11.227
You can dynamically narrow the tool set based on the task, the user, or the current workflow stage.

00:00:11.227 --> 00:00:17.322
For example, every support question may get access to the knowledge-base search tool.

00:00:17.322 --> 00:00:22.197
If the request references an order, also expose get order.

00:00:22.197 --> 00:00:28.265
If the user explicitly needs current public information, perhaps expose web search.

00:00:28.993 --> 00:00:35.425
Then apply authorization. Even if a tool is relevant, the user may not be allowed to use it.

00:00:35.425 --> 00:00:38.545
You can also change tools by stage.

00:00:38.545 --> 00:00:42.120
A planning stage might have only read-only tools.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.757
An execution stage might expose an action tool only after approval.

00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:53.605
Dynamic tool selection makes the agent's decision easier because it chooses from a relevant subset rather than the

00:00:53.605 --> 00:00:56.423
entire application toolbox.
